# The Cocoa display server's accepted differences from the X11 reference
# (tests/cocoa.sh): it draws in copy mode with Core Graphics, antialiased,
# so the edges of slanted lines, arcs and circles differ from X's (by
# about 10% more pixels than it differed when recorded), and text is
# CoreText's; drawops, patterns, fills, copies and images must match
# exactly. Format as tests/ref/tolerance.
#
# name      pixels  output
clipcopy    6000    same     # antialiased edges of slanted lines, a circle
lines       1500    same     # antialiased edges
shapes      1400    same     # antialiased edges of circles, arcs, polygons
text        -1      differs  # CoreText's fonts
